{
  "_about": [
    "Breakthrough camera (author 19.10). Edit here, then F3+T in game: no rebuild.",
    "Each shot is keyframes over the shot's own time t = 0..1. The camera looks at one focus point on the seated body",
    "and sits on a sphere around it:",
    "  az    degrees around the player: 0 = in front of the face, +90 = player's right, 180 = behind the back",
    "  pitch degrees of elevation of the camera: + = above looking down, - = below looking up (ground shot)",
    "  dist  blocks from the focus point to the camera (a wall pulls it in, never closer than 0.4)",
    "  focus height of the focus point above the player's feet (seated eyes ~0.95, lap ~0.45)",
    "  roll  dutch tilt in degrees (zero when the shake slider is 0)",
    "  fov   multiplier of the player's field of view (below 1 = a longer lens)",
    "ease: in_out | linear | in | out.  rest: the t where the shot holds when the shake slider is 0.",
    "mirror: true = the scene may turn the shot to the other side (the side with more room is chosen).",
    "plans: per target rank (1 third, 2 second, 3 first, 4 Peak) the shots in order; share = part of the scene,",
    "blend = ticks to glide in from the previous shot (0 = hard cut), flip = take the opposite side,",
    "reverse = play the shot backwards (orbit ends where the crane starts, so the two join without a cut).",
    "Scene length per rank is in Realm.breakthroughTicks (10.8 / 15.2 / 15.2 / 25.5 s; last shot holds through Realm.releaseTicks)."
  ],
